From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:54:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] unpin swig for riscv64

pyproject.toml's build-system.requires pins "swig<4.3.0". PyPI's swig
package only started publishing manylinux_riscv64 wheels at 4.3.1.post0,
so pip falls back to building swig itself from its sdist on riscv64 for
no reason that applies to this build: the pin (commit 839503b) exists to
avoid a SWIG 4.3.0 numpy.i regression that segfaulted under Python 3.8 +
pandas>2, and this release already requires Python >=3.11.

Drop the pin so pip resolves swig 4.5.1, which ships a riscv64 wheel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-only infra constraint; the pin's own Python 3.8 rationale no longer applies to this release]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 718ff67..5b6f1cc 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@ requires = [
     "numpy>=2.0.0",
     "pybind11",
     "scikit-build-core[pyproject]>=0.10",
-    "swig<4.3.0",
+    "swig",
 ]
 build-backend = "scikit_build_core.build"

